cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below."
title: "BIOS microcode CPU enablement: a Boot Guard-safe same-size microcode swap for OEM PCs"
abstract: >-
  Documentation and offline tools for running a newer Intel CPU on an OEM motherboard whose final BIOS
  lacks that CPU's microcode. The microcode is copied from the same vendor's BIOS for a sibling model into
  a same-size slot, leaving the Firmware Interface Table byte-identical and every Boot Guard-hashed byte
  unchanged. A verifier parses the Boot Policy Manifest from each image and refuses unsafe ones. Reference
  build: Dell OptiPlex 7060 SFF, BIOS 1.32.0, i7-9700T (CPUID 906ED).
type: software
authors:
  - alias: dmmdea
repository-code: "https://github.com/dmmdea/bios-microcode-cpu-enablement"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - CPU microcode
  - BIOS modification
  - Intel Boot Guard
  - Firmware Interface Table
  - OEM firmware
  - hardware reuse
  - e-waste reduction
